repository-code: 'https://github.com/gcastellazzi/aLoTiA'
url: 'https://gcastellazzi.github.io/aLoTiA/app/'
abstract: >-
  Interactive graphical statics of masonry arches in the browser. A photograph
  of a real arch is traced into voussoirs, scaled and loaded, and the line of
  thrust is then moved through its three degrees of freedom while the software
  checks, joint by joint, whether it stays inside the masonry. Where the line
  would leave the ring it stays hooked at a face, that point becomes a hinge,
  and the collapse mechanism is counted and drawn. The tool exists to make the
  infinity of admissible equilibrium states of an arch something a student can
  take hold of and move.
keywords:
  - masonry arches
  - graphical statics
  - line of thrust
  - funicular polygon
  - limit analysis
  - collapse mechanism
  - structural engineering education
  - historical structures
